## Phase 7: Lifecycle & Edge-Case Matrix

For every feature or bug fix, consider:

### Lifecycle Angle
| Stage | Question |
|-------|----------|
| Setup | How is the feature initialized? Are defaults sane? Are resources allocated safely? |
| Conflict | What happens if triggered twice or concurrently? Are locks or idempotency handled? |
| Cleanup | Are temporary/ghost resources cleaned? Does it leave stale data? |

### Paradox / "What If" Angle
| Condition | Considerations |
|-----------|---------------|
| Empty / Edge Data | Zero entries, missing fields, null values |
| Scale / Load | Tens, thousands, millions of items — memory, CPU, storage |
| Interruption / Failure | User refresh, cancel, network loss, crash |
| Security | Unauthorized access, injection, sensitive data leaks |

### Contextual Angle
| Factor | Question |
|--------|----------|
| Side Effects | Does it impact other modules, services, or scheduled jobs? |
| Dependencies | External services, databases, APIs — what if they fail? |
| Assumptions | Network speed, OS, permissions, VM uptime |

